   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>Consider the following statements for a language:<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : If every subset of <em>L</em> is decidable, then <em>L</em> must be CFL.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : If <em>L</em> is a regular language, then every subset of <em>L</em> is decidable.<br />\nWhich of the following statements is incorrect?</p>",
   "options": [
