  {
   "n": 21,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +2 / -0",
   "html": "<p>Let <em>A</em> ≤<sub><em>m</em></sub> <em>B</em> denotes that language <em>A</em> is mapping reducible to language <em>B</em>.<br />\nWhich of the following is/are true?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "If <em>A</em> ≤<sub><em>m</em></sub> B and every subset of <em>B</em> is CFL only if <em>A</em> must be finite language."
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "If <em>A</em> ≤<sub>m</sub> <em>B</em> and <em>B</em> is decidable, then <em>A</em> is closed under subset operation."
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "If <em>A</em> ≤<em><sub>m</sub></em> <em>B</em> and <em>A</em> is decidable, then <em>B</em> must be finite language."
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "If <em>A</em> ≤<em><sub>m</sub></em> <em>B</em> and every subset of <em>A</em> are decidable if <em>B</em> is finite language."
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A",
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A, D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p>(a, d)<br />\n<em>A</em> &le;<em><sub>m</sub> B</em>, power of language <em>B</em> is greater than equal to <em>A</em>.<br />\nSo, if <em>B</em> is decidable then <em>A</em> is decidable.<br />\nIf B is finite and <em>A</em> is also finite and finite languages are closed under infinite subset.</p>"
  },
